  "worked_solution": "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\n\u00acD\u2228(\u00acD\u2227C)\u2261\u00acD.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $\u00acD.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acD\u2228(C\u2227\u00acD) & \u2261\u00acD\u2228(\u00acD\u2227C) \\\\  & \u2261\u00acD.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $\u00acD.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acD\u2228(\u00acD\u2227C) & \u2261\u00acD.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $\u00acD.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
